{#
  KanbanBoard macro — a keyboard-and-pointer-accessible kanban board:
  cards move between columns via a per-card "Move to…" menu (the
  accessible path) or native HTML5 drag-and-drop (supplementary).

  HTML tag: <div> (root) wrapping a <table role="grid"> built from
            @lilydesignsystem/nunjucks-headless's kanban-table macro
            family, plus one aria-live status paragraph.
  CSS class: kanban-board
  Companion runtime: kanban-board.client.js

  This macro composes, unmodified, a real npm dependency's macros:
  lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless's kanban-table family
  (kanbanTable, kanbanTableHead, kanbanTableBody, kanbanTableRow,
  kanbanTableTh, kanbanTableTd) for the grid's structural markup — the
  same "depend on, don't vendor" rule every other Lily helper follows
  for its own headless dependency. kanban-board.client.js separately
  depends on @lilydesignsystem/nunjucks-listbox-behavior for the move
  menu's APG listbox keyboard contract.

  IMPLEMENTATION NOTE — every nested composition below is built with
  plain macro-call expressions (`{{ someMacro(args) }}`) and each
  headless macro's `html`/`attributes` params, NEVER Nunjucks'
  `{% call %}` block form for structural nesting. Empirically verified
  while building this package: a variable introduced with `{% set %}`
  in an enclosing macro body is NOT visible inside a nested
  `{% call otherMacro() %}...{% endcall %}` body (only that body's own
  loop variables and the enclosing macro's OWN parameters are) — a
  real Nunjucks scoping trap, undocumented as far as this port found.
  Building every level bottom-up as a `| safe`-marked HTML string and
  threading every value the leaf needs as an explicit macro parameter
  sidesteps it entirely. See AGENTS.md "Nunjucks gotchas".

  Every card cell's move-button + move-listbox markup is rendered
  UNCONDITIONALLY at SSR time (hidden via the `hidden` attribute and
  aria-expanded="false"), exactly the way theme-picker.njk always
  renders its listbox and merely toggles `hidden` client-side — there
  is no server-side notion of "the menu that happens to be open" the
  way the Svelte canonical's `{#if openCardId === card.id}` block has.
  One consequence worth calling out: every card's move button is a
  distinct, stable DOM node from first render onward, so there is no
  single shared "last mounted button" variable for client.js to
  mis-bind — see kanban-board.client.js's header comment and
  spec/index.md §10 for the shared-ref regression this sidesteps by
  construction (the same bug independently found and fixed in every
  other framework catalog's own port of this component).

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  NUNJUCKS DEVIATIONS from the canonical Svelte props
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. cardLabel: (card) => string in Svelte, default card.title. A
     macro cannot evaluate a callback (the established rule in this
     catalog — see date-time-picker.njk's own deviations, and
     share-picker.njk's `href`-as-string deviation). There is no
     `cardLabel` macro param: the macro always renders `card.title`.
     A consumer who wants different display text sets it on the card
     data itself before calling the macro (mirrors share-picker's
     "pass the already-resolved value" precedent).

  2. labels.cardCount / labels.overLimit / labels.moveButton: each a
     function taking numeric/card arguments in Svelte. Same reason as
     above — these deviate to TEMPLATE STRINGS with `{token}`
     placeholders the macro substitutes at render time via the
     `replace` filter:
       cardCount  — e.g. "{count} cards"            -> {count}
       overLimit  — e.g. "Over limit: {count}/{limit}" -> {count}, {limit}
       moveButton — e.g. "Move {card}"                -> {card} (the card's title)
     Every field stays optional and gates the control/text it names,
     exactly like the canonical Svelte props (absence -> "" / no render).

  3. labels.moveMenuLabel stays a plain string (it already was one in
     Svelte — no deviation needed).

  4. labels.moveAnnouncement: (cardTitle, columnTitle) => string stays
     a REAL function — but it is never called from this macro. A
     move only ever happens after hydration (drag or the move menu),
     so the announcement is entirely kanban-board.client.js's concern:
     pass it as `initKanbanBoard(root, {labels: {moveAnnouncement}})`.

  5. onMove: (cardId, toColumnId) => void — same as #4, a
     kanban-board.client.js init option, never a macro param.

  6. onReorder, canMove, labels.moveBlocked, labels.reorderAnnouncement —
     the same story as #4 and #5: all callbacks, so all
     `initKanbanBoard(root, {...})` options, never macro params.
       onReorder(cardId, toIndex)   — Alt+ArrowUp/Down within a column.
       canMove(cardId, toColumnId)  — veto; refused options get
                                      aria-disabled when the menu opens.
       labels.moveBlocked(cardTitle, columnTitle)
       labels.reorderAnnouncement(cardTitle, position, total)

  7. readonly — a plain boolean macro param (see below). It renders no
     move button, no move menu and no draggable handle, and sets
     `data-readonly` on the root; the client script also checks that
     attribute, so reorder is disabled too. Arrow-key navigation stays.

  8. Round 2 — collapse, add card, hard limits:
       columns[].strictLimit — a boolean on the column data: a move into it is
                               refused (by the client) once it holds wipLimit
                               cards. Rendered as data-strict-limit.
       collapsedColumns      — macro param, array of column ids: the toggle's
                               aria-expanded and data-collapsed render at SSR;
                               the client then keeps those columns' cards out of
                               the DOM (it needs `initKanbanBoard` to have run:
                               without it the cards stay visible).
       labels.collapseColumn / labels.expandColumn / labels.addCard — template
                               strings with a `{column}` token (the column's
                               title). Each gates the control it names; the add
                               button is never rendered when `readonly`.
       onCollapsedChange(ids), onAddCard(columnId) — client init options; the
                               client also fires `collapsechange` / `addcard`
                               events on the root.

  9. Round 3 and consumer-requested capabilities:
       card fields: subtitle, badges (array), flag, href, locked, draggable (false),
         attrs (object, extra attributes on the cell), allowedColumns (array of ids:
         the move menu lists only these and the card's own column; the client refuses
         other moves). `flag` is visible text, data-flag, and aria-describedby on the cell.
       column fields: flag, accent (data-accent), headerHtml / footerHtml (HTML strings,
         rendered in the header after the title / in a <tfoot> cell).
       labels.emptyColumn — template string with {column}: a message in an empty column.
       labels.search — plain string: renders a search field; the client filters the
         cards by title, subtitle and badges (stashed out of the DOM like a collapsed
         column; data-hidden-count on the header). `search` (macro param) is its start value.
       Client options: moveHandler(cardId, toColumnId, toIndex?) returns a promise: the
         source cell shows data-pending / aria-busy while it is pending (the client does
         not rebuild the board, so the card stays put; the consumer re-renders on success),
         then labels.moveFailed(cardTitle, columnTitle, error) / onMoveError on rejection,
         labels.movePending / labels.moveAnnouncement. onMove's third argument is the drop
         position (when a pointer drop landed on a card); a drop on a card of the card's own
         column calls onReorder(cardId, toIndex). Alt+ArrowLeft/Right moves a card to the
         neighbouring column.

  10. 0.4.0 — multi-select, undo, column reordering, swimlanes, drag preview, virtualization:
       selectable    — macro param (boolean): aria-multiselectable on the grid and `data-lily-kanban-board-selectable`
                       on the root; `selected` (array of card ids) renders data-selected / aria-selected at SSR.
                       The client toggles a card on Ctrl/Cmd+click or the `x` key and moves the whole selection together.
       undoable      — macro param (boolean); labels.undo (plain string) renders the undo button. The client keeps the
                       stack and calls onMove(cardId, fromColumnId) to take a move back. NUNJUCKS DEVIATION: the board is
                       server-rendered and the client never sees the consumer's data, so it cannot check that a card is
                       still where the move left it — the consumer ignores a stale undo.
       movableColumns / columnOrder — macro params: draggable headers (the client reorders the columns in place) and the
                       starting order (array of column ids; unnamed columns follow). The client reports the new order
                       through onColumnOrderChange(ids) and the `columnorderchange` event.
       lanes         — macro param, array<{id, title}>; card.laneId names a card's lane (the first lane when absent). Each
                       lane gets a `.kanban-board-lane` header row (th scope="rowgroup"). The client passes the lane id to
                       onMove as its fourth argument for a drop into another lane's cell.
       virtualize    — macro param {rowHeight, height, overscan?}: the table sits in a `.kanban-board-scroll` area; every
                       row is rendered at SSR (without the client script the area is just scrollable) and the client
                       keeps only the rows in view in the DOM, between `.kanban-board-spacer` rows. aria-rowindex /
                       aria-rowcount are rendered at SSR.
       Client options: dragPreviewText(cards) — cards are `{id, title}`; onSelectionChange(ids), onColumnOrderChange(ids);
         labels.moveManyAnnouncement(count, columnTitle), labels.undoAnnouncement(cardTitle, columnTitle),
         labels.undoManyAnnouncement(count), labels.columnMoveAnnouncement(columnTitle, position, count).

  11. 0.5.0 — collapsible swimlanes:
       collapsedLanes — macro param, array of lane ids: a collapsed lane keeps its `.kanban-board-lane` header row but its
                       card rows render `hidden` and the client keeps them hidden.
       labels.collapseLane / labels.expandLane — template strings with a `{lane}` token (the lane's title). Each gates the
                       `.kanban-board-lane-toggle` button (aria-expanded); either one renders it.
       labels.laneCount — template string with `{lane}` and `{count}` tokens, a visible `.kanban-board-lane-count`; the
                       client keeps the count in step with the search.
       onLaneCollapseChange(ids) — client init option; the client also fires `lanecollapsechange`, and `collapsedLanes()`
                       on the controller returns the ids. The lane title is wrapped in `.kanban-board-lane-title`.

  12. 0.6.0 — typed fields, inline editing, export:
       fields        — macro param, array<{id, header, type?, options?, editable?, editLabel?, exportable?, numberFormat?,
                       dateFormat?}>: declarative (no functions). A card's `values` object holds each field's value by id. Each
                       card cell shows `.kanban-board-card-fields` with one `.kanban-board-card-field` per field (its header,
                       then the value). The server renders the raw value (a select's option label); the client formats it by
                       type once it runs. `locale` is the BCP 47 tag for numbers and dates (never defaulted).
       editableFields — macro param (boolean): turns inline editing on (not for a readonly board or a locked card; a field with
                       `editable: false`, or of a type that cannot be edited, stays text). The value becomes a
                       `.kanban-board-field-button`. NUNJUCKS DEVIATION: a macro cannot see a client listener, so this flag
                       stands in for the other catalogs' `onFieldEdit` / `field-edit` listener. The client's
                       `initKanbanBoard(root, { onFieldEdit })` reports each accepted edit (and fires `fieldedit`).
       exportFilename / exportScope — macro params ("kanban-board" / "view" or "selected").
       labels.export, labels.exportCsv / exportTsv / exportExcel — plain strings; labels.exportHeaders — an object of plain
                       strings ({title, column, lane?, subtitle?, badges?, flag?}); none of the buttons renders without it.
       labels.exportAnnouncement — template string, tokens {count}, {format}, {filename}.
       labels.editAnnouncement  — template string, tokens {card}, {field}, {value}.
       labels.editInvalid       — template string, tokens {card}, {field}.
       labels.editRefused       — template string, tokens {card}, {field}, {message} (a field's `validate` refused the value).
       labels.fieldUndoAnnouncement / labels.fieldRedoAnnouncement — template strings, tokens {card}, {field}, {value}.
       labels.copy              — plain string: a button that puts the export (header row first, tab-separated) on the clipboard.
       labels.copyAnnouncement  — template string, token {count}; labels.copyFailed — plain string.
       labels.searchAnnouncement — template string, tokens {matched}, {total}.
       editableTitles — macro param (boolean): card titles edit in place (double-click, or F2 on the card; Enter or leaving the
                       field commits, Escape cancels, an empty title is refused; not for linked cards). NUNJUCKS DEVIATION: a macro
                       cannot see a client listener, so this flag stands in for the other catalogs' `onTitleEdit`. The client's
                       `initKanbanBoard(root, { onTitleEdit })` reports each rename ({cardId, title, previous}) and fires `titleedit`.
                       labels.titleEditor — template, token {title}: the editor's accessible name; labels.titleEditAnnouncement —
                       template, tokens {previous}, {title}.
       Client options: onFieldEdit({cardId, fieldId, value, previous}), onExport(file) (return false to take over the download), onCopy({ text, rowCount }) (return false to take over the copy).

  Params (single `opts` object):
    label       — string, required. aria-label for the grid table.
    columns     — array<{id, title, wipLimit?, strictLimit?}>, required.
    collapsedColumns — array<string>. Ids of collapsed columns.
    collapsedLanes   — array<string>. Ids of collapsed swimlanes (see 11 above).
    cards       — array<{id, columnId, title}>, required. Card order
                  within a column follows the order cards appear in
                  this array (matches the Svelte canonical).
    caption     — string. Visible <caption>, forwarded to kanbanTable.
    labels      — object. See deviations above. Every field optional;
                  its presence gates the control/text it names.
    readonly    — boolean. Disable every mutating interaction.
    selectable, selected, undoable, movableColumns, columnOrder, lanes, virtualize — see 10 above.
    name        — string, default "board". Discriminator for ids.
    id          — string, default "kanban-board-{name}".
    classes     — string. Extra CSS classes on the root <div>.
    attributes  — object. Extra HTML attributes spread onto the root.

  Custom move-button glyph: call the macro with a `{% call %}` block;
  the block body replaces the default glyph inside EVERY card's move
  button (there is one macro invocation for the whole board, unlike a
  per-card override, which no Nunjucks macro call shape supports).

  Usage:
    {% from "./kanban-board.njk" import kanbanBoard %}
    {{ kanbanBoard({
      label: "Sprint board",
      columns: [{id: "todo", title: "To do"}, {id: "done", title: "Done", wipLimit: 3}],
      cards: [{id: "c1", columnId: "todo", title: "Write the spec"}],
      labels: {
        cardCount: "{count} cards",
        overLimit: "Over limit: {count}/{limit}",
        moveButton: "Move {card}",
        moveMenuLabel: "Move to column"
      }
    }) }}

  Then load kanban-board.client.js once and call autoInit().

  Spec: spec/index.md §4 (macro parameters), §6 (behaviour).
#}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table/macro.njk" import kanbanTable %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table-head/macro.njk" import kanbanTableHead %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table-body/macro.njk" import kanbanTableBody %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table-row/macro.njk" import kanbanTableRow %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table-th/macro.njk" import kanbanTableTh %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/kanban-table-td/macro.njk" import kanbanTableTd %}

{%- macro _kanbanBoardHeaderCellHtml(column, count, overLimit, labels, collapsed, readonly) -%}
{%- if labels.collapseColumn or labels.expandColumn %}<button type="button" class="kanban-board-collapse-button" aria-expanded="{{ 'false' if collapsed else 'true' }}" aria-label="{{ (labels.expandColumn if collapsed else labels.collapseColumn) | default(labels.collapseColumn) | replace('{column}', column.title) }}" data-lily-kanban-board-collapse data-lily-kanban-board-column-id="{{ column.id }}">{{ '▸' if collapsed else '▾' }}</button>{% endif -%}
{{- column.title -}}
{%- if column.flag %}<span class="kanban-board-column-flag">{{ column.flag }}</span>{% endif -%}
{%- if column.headerHtml %}{{ column.headerHtml | safe }}{% endif -%}
{%- if labels.cardCount %}<span class="kanban-board-count">{{ labels.cardCount | replace("{count}", count) }}</span>{% endif -%}
{%- if overLimit and labels.overLimit %}<span class="kanban-board-wip-warning">{{ labels.overLimit | replace("{count}", count) | replace("{limit}", column.wipLimit) }}</span>{% endif -%}
{%- if labels.addCard and not readonly %}<button type="button" class="kanban-board-add-button" aria-label="{{ labels.addCard | replace('{column}', column.title) }}" data-lily-kanban-board-add data-lily-kanban-board-column-id="{{ column.id }}">+</button>{% endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro _kanbanBoardCardCellHtml(card, columns, labels, id, glyphHtml, readonly, emptyText, fields, editableFields) -%}
{%- if card -%}
{%- set moveListId = id + "-move-list-" + card.id -%}
{%- set moveButtonId = id + "-move-button-" + card.id -%}
{%- set movable = (not readonly) and (not card.locked) -%}
{#- The move button only when labels.moveButton names it: an unnamed button is
    worse than none, and Enter/Space on the cell opens the menu either way. The
    menu is named by the card itself when no moveMenuLabel is given. -#}
<span class="kanban-board-card-title"{% if movable and card.draggable != false %} draggable="true"{% endif %} data-lily-kanban-board-card-handle data-lily-kanban-board-card-id="{{ card.id }}">{% if card.href %}<a class="kanban-board-card-link" href="{{ card.href }}">{{ card.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ card.title }}{% endif %}</span>
{%- if card.subtitle %}<span class="kanban-board-card-subtitle">{{ card.subtitle }}</span>{% endif -%}
{%- if card.badges and card.badges | length %}<span class="kanban-board-card-badges">{% for badge in card.badges %}<span class="kanban-board-card-badge">{{ badge }}</span>{% endfor %}</span>{% endif -%}
{%- if fields | length %}<span class="kanban-board-card-fields">
{%- for f in fields -%}
  {%- set raw = (card.values[f.id]) if card.values else "" -%}
  {%- set text = "" -%}
  {%- if raw is defined and raw is not none and raw != "" -%}
    {%- set text = raw | string -%}
    {%- if f.options -%}{%- for o in f.options -%}{%- if o.id == raw -%}{%- set text = o.label -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- set ftype = f.type | default("text") -%}
  {%- set fieldEditable = editableFields and movable and (f.editable != false) and (ftype in ["text", "number", "link", "date", "time", "select", "radio"]) -%}
  {%- if text != "" or fieldEditable -%}
  <span class="kanban-board-card-field" data-field="{{ f.id }}" data-type="{{ ftype }}" data-lily-kanban-board-field><span class="kanban-board-card-field-name" id="{{ id }}-fn-{{ card.id }}-{{ f.id }}">{{ f.header }}</span> {% if fieldEditable %}<button type="button" class="kanban-board-field-button" id="{{ id }}-fv-{{ card.id }}-{{ f.id }}" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="{{ id }}-fn-{{ card.id }}-{{ f.id }} {{ id }}-fv-{{ card.id }}-{{ f.id }}" data-lily-kanban-board-field-button data-lily-kanban-board-card-id="{{ card.id }}" data-field-id="{{ f.id }}">{{ text }}</button>{% else %}<span class="kanban-board-card-field-value">{{ text }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
</span>{% endif -%}
{%- if card.flag %}<span class="kanban-board-card-flag" id="{{ id }}-flag-{{ card.id }}">{{ card.flag }}</span>{% endif -%}
{%- if movable %}{% if labels.moveButton %}<button type="button" class="kanban-board-move-button" id="{{ moveButtonId }}" tabindex="-1" aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="{{ moveListId }}" aria-label="{{ labels.moveButton | replace('{card}', card.title) }}" data-lily-kanban-board-move-button data-lily-kanban-board-card-id="{{ card.id }}">{{ glyphHtml | safe }}</button>{% endif %}<ul class="kanban-board-move-list" id="{{ moveListId }}" role="listbox" aria-label="{{ labels.moveMenuLabel | default(card.title) }}" tabindex="-1" hidden data-lily-kanban-board-move-list data-lily-kanban-board-card-id="{{ card.id }}">{%- for destination in columns -%}{%- if (not card.allowedColumns) or destination.id == card.columnId or destination.id in card.allowedColumns -%}<li class="kanban-board-move-option" id="{{ id }}-move-option-{{ card.id }}-{{ loop.index0 }}" role="option" aria-selected="{{ 'true' if destination.id == card.columnId else 'false' }}" data-value="{{ destination.id }}">{{ destination.title }}</li>{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}</ul>{% endif %}
{%- elif emptyText -%}
<span class="kanban-board-empty">{{ emptyText }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro _kanbanBoardHeaderRowHtml(columns, columnCardLists, labels, collapsedColumns, readonly, movableColumns) -%}
{%- set out = "" -%}
{%- for column in columns -%}
  {%- set colCards = columnCardLists[loop.index0] -%}
  {%- set count = colCards.length -%}
  {%- set overLimit = column.wipLimit is defined and column.wipLimit is not none and count > column.wipLimit -%}
  {%- set thAttrs = [["data-lily-kanban-board-column-id", column.id], ["data-lily-kanban-board-column-title", column.title]] -%}
  {%- if movableColumns -%}{%- set thAttrs = thAttrs.concat([["draggable", "true"]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if column.flag -%}{%- set thAttrs = thAttrs.concat([["data-flag", column.flag]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if column.accent -%}{%- set thAttrs = thAttrs.concat([["data-accent", column.accent]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if overLimit -%}{%- set thAttrs = thAttrs.concat([["data-over-limit", ""]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- set collapsed = column.id in collapsedColumns -%}
  {%- if collapsed -%}{%- set thAttrs = thAttrs.concat([["data-collapsed", ""]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if column.strictLimit and column.wipLimit is defined and column.wipLimit is not none -%}{%- set thAttrs = thAttrs.concat([["data-strict-limit", ""], ["data-wip-limit", column.wipLimit]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- set cellHtml = _kanbanBoardHeaderCellHtml(column, count, overLimit, labels, collapsed, readonly) -%}
  {%- set out = (out ~ kanbanTableTh({ attributes: thAttrs, html: cellHtml })) | safe -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- out | safe -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro _kanbanBoardBodyRowHtml(rowIndex, laneRow, columns, columnCardLists, labels, id, glyphHtml, readonly, collapsedColumns, selected, hasLanes, fields, editableFields) -%}
{%- set out = "" -%}
{%- for column in columns -%}
  {%- set colIndex = loop.index0 -%}
  {%- set colCards = columnCardLists[colIndex] -%}
  {%- set card = colCards[laneRow] -%}
  {%- set isActive = (rowIndex == 0 and colIndex == 0) -%}
  {%- set tdAttrs = [["data-row", rowIndex], ["data-col", colIndex], ["tabindex", (0 if isActive else -1)]] -%}
  {%- if column.accent -%}{%- set tdAttrs = tdAttrs.concat([["data-accent", column.accent]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if card -%}
    {%- set tdAttrs = tdAttrs.concat([["data-lily-kanban-board-card-id", card.id], ["data-lily-kanban-board-search-text", (card.title ~ " " ~ (card.subtitle | default("")) ~ " " ~ ((card.badges | default([])) | join(" ")))]]) -%}
    {%- if card.locked -%}{%- set tdAttrs = tdAttrs.concat([["data-locked", ""]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if card.id in selected -%}{%- set tdAttrs = tdAttrs.concat([["data-selected", ""], ["aria-selected", "true"]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if card.flag -%}{%- set tdAttrs = tdAttrs.concat([["data-flag", card.flag], ["aria-describedby", id + "-flag-" + card.id]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if card.allowedColumns -%}{%- set tdAttrs = tdAttrs.concat([["data-lily-kanban-board-allowed-columns", card.allowedColumns | join(",")]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if card.attrs -%}{%- for attrName, attrValue in card.attrs -%}{%- set tdAttrs = tdAttrs.concat([[attrName, attrValue]]) -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- set emptyText = (labels.emptyColumn | replace("{column}", column.title)) if ((not hasLanes) and rowIndex == 0 and not card and labels.emptyColumn and colCards.length == 0 and not (column.id in collapsedColumns)) else "" -%}
  {%- if emptyText -%}{%- set tdAttrs = tdAttrs.concat([["data-empty", ""]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- set cellHtml = _kanbanBoardCardCellHtml(card, columns, labels, id, glyphHtml, readonly, emptyText, fields, editableFields) -%}
  {%- set out = (out ~ kanbanTableTd({ attributes: tdAttrs, html: cellHtml })) | safe -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- out | safe -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro kanbanBoard(opts) -%}
{%- set columns = opts.columns -%}
{#- Display order: the columns `columnOrder` names first, the rest after in their own order. -#}
{%- set columnOrder = opts.columnOrder | default([]) -%}
{%- if columnOrder | length -%}
  {%- set orderedColumns = [] -%}
  {%- for orderedId in columnOrder -%}{%- for column in opts.columns -%}{%- if column.id == orderedId -%}{%- set orderedColumns = orderedColumns.concat([column]) -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endfor -%}
  {%- for column in opts.columns -%}{%- if not (column.id in columnOrder) -%}{%- set orderedColumns = orderedColumns.concat([column]) -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
  {%- set columns = orderedColumns -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set lanes = opts.lanes | default([]) -%}
{%- set hasLanes = (lanes | length) > 0 -%}
{%- set selectedIds = opts.selected | default([]) -%}
{%- set fieldDefs = opts.fields | default([]) -%}
{%- set cards = opts.cards -%}
{%- set labels = opts.labels | default({}) -%}
{%- set name = opts.name | default("board") -%}
{%- set id = opts.id | default("kanban-board-" + name) -%}
{%- set statusId = id + "-status" -%}
{%- set hasCustomGlyph = caller is defined -%}
{%- set glyphHtml = (caller() if hasCustomGlyph else '<span aria-hidden="true">&#8644;</span>') | safe -%}
{#- Group cards by column, preserving each card's position in `cards`,
    and find the tallest column — the "sparse but rectangular" grid
    trade-off documented in spec/helpers/index.md. Built with
    `.concat()` accumulation rather than a dict/selectattr filter —
    see AGENTS.md "Nunjucks gotchas" for why selectattr("x","equalto",v)
    did not reliably filter in this Nunjucks version. -#}
{%- set columnCardLists = [] -%}
{%- set maxRows = 0 -%}
{%- for column in columns -%}
  {%- set colCards = [] -%}
  {%- for card in cards -%}
    {%- if card.columnId == column.id -%}
      {%- set colCards = colCards.concat([card]) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- set columnCardLists = columnCardLists.concat([colCards]) -%}
  {%- if colCards.length > maxRows -%}{%- set maxRows = colCards.length -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set collapsedIds = opts.collapsedColumns | default([]) -%}
{%- set collapsedLaneIds = opts.collapsedLanes | default([]) -%}
{%- set headerRowHtml = _kanbanBoardHeaderRowHtml(columns, columnCardLists, labels, collapsedIds, opts.readonly, opts.movableColumns) -%}
{%- set theadHtml = (kanbanTableHead({ html: (kanbanTableRow({ html: headerRowHtml }) | safe) })) | safe -%}
{#- Rows: one band per lane (a single anonymous band without `lanes`). `rowIndex` runs across lanes, `laneRow` within one. -#}
{%- set bands = lanes if hasLanes else [{ id: "", title: "" }] -%}
{%- set bodyRowsHtml = "" -%}
{%- set rowIndex = 0 -%}
{%- set slotIndex = 0 -%}
{%- for lane in bands -%}
  {%- set laneLists = [] -%}
  {%- set laneRows = 0 -%}
  {%- for column in columns -%}
    {%- set laneCards = [] -%}
    {%- for card in cards -%}
      {%- if card.columnId == column.id and ((not hasLanes) or (card.laneId | default(lanes[0].id)) == lane.id) -%}
        {%- set laneCards = laneCards.concat([card]) -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- set laneLists = laneLists.concat([laneCards]) -%}
    {%- if laneCards.length > laneRows -%}{%- set laneRows = laneCards.length -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {#- A lane keeps at least one row so a card can be dropped into it; without lanes a row exists for an
      empty column's message even when no column has a card. -#}
  {%- if hasLanes and laneRows == 0 -%}{%- set laneRows = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if (not hasLanes) and laneRows == 0 and labels.emptyColumn and columns | length -%}{%- set laneRows = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- set laneCollapsed = hasLanes and (lane.id in collapsedLaneIds) -%}
  {%- if hasLanes -%}
    {%- set laneTotal = 0 -%}
    {%- for list in laneLists -%}{%- set laneTotal = laneTotal + list.length -%}{%- endfor -%}
    {%- set laneToggleHtml = "" -%}
    {%- if labels.collapseLane or labels.expandLane -%}
      {%- set laneToggleHtml = '<button type="button" class="kanban-board-lane-toggle" aria-expanded="' ~ ('false' if laneCollapsed else 'true') ~ '" aria-label="' ~ (((labels.expandLane if laneCollapsed else labels.collapseLane) | default(labels.collapseLane) | replace('{lane}', lane.title)) | e) ~ '" data-lily-kanban-board-lane-collapse data-lily-kanban-board-lane-id="' ~ (lane.id | e) ~ '" data-collapse-template="' ~ ((labels.collapseLane | default(labels.expandLane)) | e) ~ '" data-expand-template="' ~ ((labels.expandLane | default(labels.collapseLane)) | e) ~ '">' ~ ('▸' if laneCollapsed else '▾') ~ '</button>' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- set laneCountHtml = "" -%}
    {%- if labels.laneCount -%}
      {%- set laneCountHtml = '<span class="kanban-board-lane-count" data-lily-kanban-board-lane-count data-template="' ~ (labels.laneCount | e) ~ '" data-lane-title="' ~ (lane.title | e) ~ '">' ~ ((labels.laneCount | replace('{lane}', lane.title) | replace('{count}', laneTotal)) | e) ~ '</span>' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- set laneThHtml = ('<th class="kanban-board-lane" scope="rowgroup" colspan="' ~ (columns | length) ~ '" data-lane-id="' ~ (lane.id | e) ~ '"' ~ (' data-collapsed=""' if laneCollapsed else '') ~ '>' ~ laneToggleHtml ~ '<span class="kanban-board-lane-title">' ~ (lane.title | e) ~ '</span>' ~ laneCountHtml ~ '</th>') | safe -%}
    {%- set laneAttrs = [["data-lily-kanban-board-lane-row", ""]] -%}
    {%- if opts.virtualize -%}{%- set laneAttrs = laneAttrs.concat([["aria-rowindex", slotIndex + 2]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- set bodyRowsHtml = (bodyRowsHtml ~ kanbanTableRow({ attributes: laneAttrs, html: laneThHtml })) | safe -%}
    {%- set slotIndex = slotIndex + 1 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- for laneRow in range(0, laneRows) -%}
    {%- set rowCellsHtml = _kanbanBoardBodyRowHtml(rowIndex, laneRow, columns, laneLists, labels, id, glyphHtml, opts.readonly, collapsedIds, selectedIds, hasLanes, fieldDefs, opts.editableFields) -%}
    {%- set rowAttrs = [] -%}
    {%- if hasLanes -%}{%- set rowAttrs = rowAttrs.concat([["data-lane-id", lane.id], ["data-lane-row", laneRow]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if laneCollapsed -%}{%- set rowAttrs = rowAttrs.concat([["hidden", ""]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if opts.virtualize -%}{%- set rowAttrs = rowAttrs.concat([["aria-rowindex", slotIndex + 2]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- set bodyRowsHtml = (bodyRowsHtml ~ kanbanTableRow({ attributes: rowAttrs, html: rowCellsHtml })) | safe -%}
    {%- set rowIndex = rowIndex + 1 -%}
    {%- set slotIndex = slotIndex + 1 -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set tbodyHtml = (kanbanTableBody({ html: bodyRowsHtml })) | safe -%}
{%- set tfootHtml = "" -%}
{%- set hasFooter = false -%}
{%- for column in columns -%}{%- if column.footerHtml -%}{%- set hasFooter = true -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if hasFooter -%}
  {%- set tfootHtml = '<tfoot class="kanban-table-foot"><tr class="kanban-table-row">' -%}
  {%- for column in columns -%}{%- set tfootHtml = tfootHtml ~ '<td class="kanban-table-td kanban-board-column-footer"' ~ (' data-accent="' ~ column.accent ~ '"' if column.accent else '') ~ '>' ~ (column.footerHtml if column.footerHtml else '') ~ '</td>' -%}{%- endfor -%}
  {%- set tfootHtml = tfootHtml ~ '</tr></tfoot>' -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set searchHtml = ('<input type="search" class="kanban-board-search" aria-label="' ~ labels.search ~ '" value="' ~ (opts.search | default("")) ~ '" data-lily-kanban-board-search>') if labels.search else "" -%}
{%- set tableAttrs = [["role", "grid"]] -%}
{%- if opts.selectable -%}{%- set tableAttrs = tableAttrs.concat([["aria-multiselectable", "true"]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if opts.virtualize -%}{%- set tableAttrs = tableAttrs.concat([["aria-rowcount", slotIndex + 1]]) -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- set tableHtml = kanbanTable({ label: opts.label, caption: opts.caption, attributes: tableAttrs, html: (theadHtml ~ tbodyHtml ~ tfootHtml) | safe }) -%}
{#- The scroll area is structural: a virtualized board gets a fixed height and the client keeps only the rows in view. -#}
{%- if opts.virtualize -%}
  {%- set scrollHtml = ('<div class="kanban-board-scroll" style="height: ' ~ opts.virtualize.height ~ 'px; overflow: auto" data-lily-kanban-board-virtualize data-row-height="' ~ opts.virtualize.rowHeight ~ '" data-overscan="' ~ (opts.virtualize.overscan | default(3)) ~ '">' ~ tableHtml ~ '</div>') | safe -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- set scrollHtml = ('<div class="kanban-board-body">' ~ tableHtml ~ '</div>') | safe -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set exportHtml = "" -%}
{%- if labels.exportHeaders and (labels.copy or labels.exportCsv or labels.exportTsv or labels.exportExcel) -%}
  {%- set exportHtml = '<div class="kanban-board-export" role="group"' ~ ((' aria-label="' ~ (labels.export | e) ~ '"') if labels.export else '') ~ ' data-lily-kanban-board-export-group>' -%}
  {%- if labels.copy -%}{%- set exportHtml = exportHtml ~ '<button type="button" class="kanban-board-export-button" data-kanban-export-format="copy"' ~ ('' if cards | length else ' disabled') ~ '>' ~ (labels.copy | e) ~ '</button>' -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if labels.exportCsv -%}{%- set exportHtml = exportHtml ~ '<button type="button" class="kanban-board-export-button" data-kanban-export-format="csv"' ~ ('' if cards | length else ' disabled') ~ '>' ~ (labels.exportCsv | e) ~ '</button>' -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if labels.exportTsv -%}{%- set exportHtml = exportHtml ~ '<button type="button" class="kanban-board-export-button" data-kanban-export-format="tsv"' ~ ('' if cards | length else ' disabled') ~ '>' ~ (labels.exportTsv | e) ~ '</button>' -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if labels.exportExcel -%}{%- set exportHtml = exportHtml ~ '<button type="button" class="kanban-board-export-button" data-kanban-export-format="xlsx"' ~ ('' if cards | length else ' disabled') ~ '>' ~ (labels.exportExcel | e) ~ '</button>' -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- set exportHtml = exportHtml ~ '</div>' -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set configJson = ({ fields: fieldDefs, locale: opts.locale, editableFields: opts.editableFields, editableTitles: opts.editableTitles, exportFilename: opts.exportFilename | default("kanban-board"), exportScope: opts.exportScope | default("view"), columns: opts.columns, lanes: lanes, cards: cards, labels: { exportHeaders: labels.exportHeaders, exportAnnouncement: labels.exportAnnouncement, editAnnouncement: labels.editAnnouncement, editInvalid: labels.editInvalid, editRefused: labels.editRefused, fieldUndoAnnouncement: labels.fieldUndoAnnouncement, fieldRedoAnnouncement: labels.fieldRedoAnnouncement, copyAnnouncement: labels.copyAnnouncement, copyFailed: labels.copyFailed, searchAnnouncement: labels.searchAnnouncement, titleEditor: labels.titleEditor, titleEditAnnouncement: labels.titleEditAnnouncement } } | dump) -%}
{%- set undoHtml = ('<button type="button" class="kanban-board-undo-button" disabled data-lily-kanban-board-undo>' ~ (labels.undo | e) ~ '</button>') if (opts.undoable and labels.undo and not opts.readonly) else "" -%}
<div
  class="kanban-board{% if opts.classes %} {{ opts.classes }}{% endif %}"
  data-lily-kanban-board-root
  data-lily-kanban-board-name="{{ name }}"
  data-lily-kanban-board-config="{{ configJson }}"
  {%- if opts.readonly %} data-readonly{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.selectable %} data-lily-kanban-board-selectable{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.undoable %} data-lily-kanban-board-undoable{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.movableColumns %} data-lily-kanban-board-movable-columns{% endif %}
  {%- if hasLanes %} data-lily-kanban-board-has-lanes{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.attributes %}{% for k, v in opts.attributes %} {{ k }}="{{ v }}"{% endfor %}{% endif %}
>
{{ searchHtml | safe }}{{ exportHtml | safe }}{{ undoHtml | safe }}{{ scrollHtml | safe }}
<p class="kanban-board-status" id="{{ statusId }}" aria-live="polite" data-lily-kanban-board-status></p>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
